  "body": "## What changed\n\nNative **system tray app** (`mcc-desktop`) that controls the MCC server as a child process, with a persisted `~/.fcc/desktop.json` and optional startup-at-login.\n\n- **Tray menu**: Open Admin · Check Server Status · Restart Server · Start at Login (toggle) · Tray Enabled (toggle) · Quit.\n- **Config persistence**: `~/.fcc/desktop.json` (`tray_enabled`, `start_at_login`, `minimize_to_tray`, `server_auto_start`), atomic write, never raises on corrupt/missing.\n- **Startup-at-login**: Windows HKCU Run key (`winreg`), macOS LaunchAgent plist, Linux `~/.config/autostart/*.desktop`.\n- **Three surfaces**: the tray toggles, the CLI (`mcc-desktop --start-at-login/--no-start-at-login/--tray-enabled/--no-tray-enabled/--status/--export-icon`), and a minimal \"Desktop\" card on the dashboard (via `GET/POST /admin/api/desktop`).\n- **Architecture**: the tray is a thin controller that spawns `mcc-server` as a child and drives it over the loopback admin API — no in-process supervisor (our fork has none).\n- **Placeholder \"MC\" icon** at `assets/app-icon.png`, cleanly swappable when the real logo is provided.\n\nBuilt with `/ui-ux-pro-max:ui-ux-pro-max` + `/ui-ux-pro-max:brand`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Full suite: **3996 passed / 6 failed** (6 = pre-existing PowerShell-installer baseline).\n- `ruff format --check`, `ruff check`, `ty check`: clean.\n- 27 new desktop tests (persistence round-trip, corrupt-file tolerance, per-OS autostart construction).\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- `tray_enabled=false` only gates the *next* launch (a running tray can't remove its own icon portably).\n- The server persists the JSON but never applies the OS autostart (headless-safe); the next tray/CLI launch reconciles.\n- Wayland tray support is best-effort (pystray is X11-oriented).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
